LESSON 7: DEBUGGING SEARCHTERM UPDATES IN REACT
================================================================================


LESSON OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This lesson covers how to debug the SearchBar flow and verify that:

- searchTerm state updates correctly
- Props are passed correctly
- Event handlers are called
- API URL contains the correct search term
- API requests are sent successfully
- API responses contain book data
- Loading and error states work correctly


================================================================================
1. WHAT IS DEBUGGING?
================================================================================

Debugging is the process of finding and fixing problems in an application.

Common debugging tools:

- console.log()
- console.warn()
- console.error()
- Browser DevTools
- Network tab
- React DevTools
- Breakpoints
- Temporary debug UI


