8. DEBUG useEffect()
================================================================================

For the initial API call:

useEffect(() => {

  console.log(
    'Initial book fetch'
  );

  fetchBooks('javascript');

}, []);


If you specifically want to observe searchTerm:

useEffect(() => {

  console.log(
    'searchTerm changed:',
    searchTerm
  );

}, [searchTerm]);


Difference:

[]
-> Runs after initial mount

[searchTerm]
-> Runs when searchTerm changes


